CS 101 - Week 3 Notes

Today we covered functions in Python. A function is a reusable block of code
that takes inputs (called parameters) and can return an output.

We also talked about loops. A for loop repeats an action a fixed number of
times, while a while loop repeats until a condition becomes false.

Dictionaries store key-value pairs and are very useful for looking things up
quickly, similar to a real dictionary where you look up a word to find its
definition.
